From 26687a888512aec0bea7eb00b72580a127d9e3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pradeep Kumar Chitrapu <quic_pradeepc@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Feb 2025 15:59:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:CP: wifi: ath12k: 11s MLO Test framework implementation

This commit implements host driver changes to validate firmware
support for the 11s Mesh MLO use case. It handles two
independent SLO Mesh VAPs on different bands in userspace and
configures them as MLO VAPs within the driver. Currently, only
open security is supported, with secure mode support to be
added in future patches.

The framework includes the following features:
1. Handles mesh operations from userspace, adding MLO parameters
   via custom debugfs, and follows the MLO sequence for
   interface bring up and bring down.
2. Follows the peer creation and association sequences, adding
   partner link information as expected by the firmware for MLO
   connections.
3. Manages address translation and primary UMAC selection for
   traffic.
4. Uses the compilation flag `CPTCFG_ATH12K_TEST_FW_FOR_11S_MLO`,
   which is disabled by default.

Configurations for 2-link MLO in 2-node mesh:

1. Enable `ATH12K_TEST_FW_FOR_11S_MLO` in make menuconfig and recompile.
2. Define MAC addresses to be used intesting in the following format
   on both mesh nodes. For Node1, link_sta will be Node2' netdevices
   and viceversa.

    echo "<link_sta1_mac> <link_id1> <link_idx1> <vdev_id1> <is_primary_link1> <is_assoc_link1>
    <link_sta2_mac> <link_id2> <link_idx2> <vdev_id2> <is_primary_link2> <is_assoc_link2> <sta_mld_mac>
    <iface_mld_mac>" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/qcn9274\ hw2.0_0001:01:00.0/test_mlo_mesh

3. Define MAC addresses for two independent Mesh VAPs on two bands
   in `/etc/config/wireless` using `option macaddr`. MLD address is
   picked from the above debugfs.
4. Block beacons until both VAPs come up:
        echo "block" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/qcn9274\ hw2.0_0001:01:00.0/tmm_options
5. Bring up WiFi.
6. Wait until both independent SLO Mesh VAPs come up.
7. Enable beacons on both Mesh nodes and wait for association:
        echo "enable" > /sys/kernel/debug/ath12k/qcn9274\ hw2.0_0001:01:00.0/tmm_options
8. Keep only primay link's netdevice under the bridge and remove the other:
        brctl delif br-lan phy00.0-0
9. Assign IP to br-lan interface
10. Test ping.

Patch-dependency: none

Signed-off-by: Ganesh Kariganuru Mahabalesh <quic_gkarigan@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Pradeep Kumar Chitrapu <quic_pradeepc@quicinc.com>
